        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(tui): surface safe tool-validation abort diagnostics",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen the model repeatedly emitted invalid tool arguments and the run aborted, both TUI backends showed only `run aborted`. The useful validation context was lost between the tool result, terminal lifecycle event, Gateway chat projection, and TUI renderer. This closes #90982.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nCarry a typed `argument-validation` discriminator from the agent loop and prepare a static, argument-free diagnostic at the tool boundary. Gateway and embedded runs retain that safe summary through explicit aborts and lifecycle self-aborts, while arbitrary tool output, validator paths, custom messages, and echoed arguments remain private. Terminal chat projection now uses the canonical agent-run outcome so cancellation cannot downgrade timeouts or failures.\n\nThe additive `ChatAbortedEvent.errorMessage` field is propagated through the generated Swift model with a defaulted `nil` initializer parameter for source compatibility.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThe TUI now reports a concise message such as `run aborted: edit tool validation failed: invalid arguments` in both Gateway and `--local` modes. Existing successful, failed, timed-out, and cancelled terminal semantics remain unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- focused agent-core, protocol, agent lifecycle/tool, Gateway abort/chat, and both TUI projection suites: passed\n- real Gateway PTY validation-loop abort: passed\n- real local embedded PTY validation-loop abort: passed\n- `pnpm build`: passed\n- generated protocol artifacts refreshed and Swift optional initializer compatibility verified\n- fresh Codex autoreview: passed with no actionable findings\n\nNo raw model arguments or validator detail text are present in the emitted tool, lifecycle, chat, or terminal output.\n",
        "branch": "fix/90982-tui-abort-tool-error-summary",
